WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.000
The face that changed when you turned it. Peter Thompson, 1980.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:14.000
An upside-down face can hide an odd detail. The Thatcher illusion.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:21.000
Turn it upright. The alteration becomes clearer. Eyes and mouth have been rotated.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:28.000
This is not a magic trick. Orientation changes how facial features are processed.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:34.000
A real effect. A limited claim. Our schematic isn't a lab demonstration.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:40.000
Follow the evidence. Final Vestige's Mind and Perception Archive.
